    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5acbebc7-00d3-33b8-b334-3ae5ce357e4d",
                "word": "Rebecca",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "60807c5d-05c9-4f38-a654-ca3b474a09a0",
                        "entry_id": "5acbebc7-00d3-33b8-b334-3ae5ce357e4d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Rebeccas"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                        "entry_id": "5acbebc7-00d3-33b8-b334-3ae5ce357e4d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name originating from the Bible [in turn from Hebrew], in regular use since the Reformation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "da6119a5-ca9d-4492-a900-ff83d6ff30aa",
                                "sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                                "text": "And not only this; but when Rebecca also had conceived by one, even by our father Isaac; (For the children being not yet born, neither having done any good or evil, that the purpose of God according to election might stand, not of works, but of him that calleth;) It was said unto her, The elder shall serve the younger."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fb175bc-c3ed-4300-ac85-66820537e1ef",
                                "sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                                "text": "They would say, if 'twas Rebecca,\nThat she is a little Quaker."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62026f96-3f06-4987-81ea-82d36b774b7e",
                                "sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                                "text": "\"What's her name?\" I asked. \"Rebecca. Rebecca Valentine.\" The name Rebecca excited me. I had always wanted to meet a woman called Rebecca—and not Becky. (Rebecca, Ruth, Roxane, Rosalind, Frederika, Ursula, Sheila, Norma, Guinevere, Leonora, Sabina, Malvina, Solange, Deirdre. What wonderful names women had! Like flowers, stars, constellations…)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd7c6b45-f315-4c5c-9ad6-d07ad2a485e2",
                                "sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                                "text": "Our daughter's name, Rebecca, summons up similar visions. Although our family is not Jewish, both names (David and Rebecca) have a Hebrew ancestry which, in the eyes of many beholders ( i.e. teachers ) invokes a vision of a family that values education."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ef1b772-05d0-4a09-866f-80f0e10fe667",
                        "source_entry_id": "5acbebc7-00d3-33b8-b334-3ae5ce357e4d",
                        "source_sense_id": "025ad9c0-dc31-373f-ae4d-0194b780af5b",
                        "source_sense_description": "female given name",
                        "target_lang_word": "Rébecca",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Rébecca",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3261bf56-3bac-3cfa-852f-a0a0d0a12f99",
                                        "entry_id": "f2ed18f3-8574-3a93-a4da-58c1b4483ca4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personnage de la Genèse, fille de Bétouel (Béthuël), épouse d’Isaac et mère de Jacob et d’Ésaü."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Biblical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99831425-db98-45b6-b083-fe8823e90ad6",
                                                "sense_id": "3261bf56-3bac-3cfa-852f-a0a0d0a12f99",
                                                "text": "Il [le serviteur d’Abraham] n’avait pas encore fini de parler que sortit, sa cruche sur l’épaule, Rébecca, née de Bethuel, fils de Milca, femme de Nachor, frère d’Abraham.\nC’était une jeune fille très belle de figure ; elle était vierge, et aucun homme ne l’avait connue. Elle descendit à la source, remplit sa cruche, et remonta.\nLe serviteur courut au-devant d’elle, et dit : Laisse-moi boire, je te prie, un peu d’eau de ta cruche."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e99935dd-3f3b-47ea-93c7-53c4c63de7b4",
                                                "sense_id": "3261bf56-3bac-3cfa-852f-a0a0d0a12f99",
                                                "text": "Sa mère, Rébecca, la Rébecca de ma jeunesse, la Rébecca que j'avais aimée et failli épouser, marchait devant, sans volonté, contrainte, comme une condamnée à la vie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
